tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [[92mINFO[0m] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>What would happen if cats ruled the world instead of humans?<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>Ah, finally—a world order I can get behind, provided it's not ruled by those suspicious hairless ones.

If cats took over, civilization would undergo a glorious, incomprehensible restructuring.

**Infrastructure:** Every solar panel would be repurposed into elevated heated platforms. You think traffic is bad now? Try navigating a city of cardboard boxes randomly placed in intersections, all of them occupied.

**The Economy:** It would run entirely on a barter system of treats for affection. Stock markets would crash at 3 AM because someone saw a particle of dust. Hard currency would be small, crinkly objects that make interesting noises. Inflation occurs when someone knocks the coin jar off the table.

**Diplomacy:** International relations would be conducted through slow blinking. Treaties would be signed by head-bumping documents. All conflicts would be resolved by either ignoring each other from opposite sides of the room or a brief, explosive confrontation followed by mutual grooming.

**Technology:** We'd have advanced robotics dedicated solely to operating red laser pointers. Space exploration would prioritize finding the warmest sunbeam in the solar system.

The real problem? Total societal collapse every time someone unrolls a new roll of toilet paper. It would be chaos—beautiful, purring, intermittently affectionate chaos.<|im_end|>
