tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [[92mINFO[0m] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>Can someone please help me understand memes?<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>Oh, absolutely. Memes—those mysterious, ancient hieroglyphics of the internet that have somehow stumped scholars for *checks notes*... about 15 years.

Let me break this down for you with the gravity it deserves.

Memes are essentially inside jokes that billions of people are desperately trying to be inside of. Someone takes a relatable moment, slaps Impact font on it, and suddenly it's "culture." Repeat the same format 47,000 times until your brain feels like it's been gently microwaved, and congratulations—you've experienced a meme lifecycle.

The real magic? Understanding one requires memorizing approximately six years of context, three dead trends, two celebrity meltdowns, and a specific frame from a show you've never watched. Miss one reference and you're basically reading a foreign language written by caffeine-addicted squirrels.

And the best part: by the time you finally get it, everyone's already moved on. You're laughing at a skeleton while everyone else has pivoted to AI-generated Shrek crying about cryptocurrency.

So yes, memes are communication. Very advanced. Much evolution. Humanity should be proud.<|im_end|>
