tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [[92mINFO[0m] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>Create a motivational speech for someone struggling with motivation.<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>Oh boy, a motivational speech for the unmotivated. The irony is *chef's kiss*.

---

**"The Glorious Art of Doing Absolutely Nothing"**

Look at you—standing at the crossroads of "maybe tomorrow" and "why bother." Truly inspiring stuff. You've turned procrastination into a lifestyle, and honestly? The commitment is remarkable. Most people can't maintain that level of enthusiastic indifference. You're basically an athlete at this point.

Here's the thing nobody tells you: motivation is a scam. A flaky friend who shows up late, leaves early, and raids your fridge. Meanwhile, discipline is the boring roommate who actually pays rent on time. You don't *wait* for inspiration to strike like lightning—you plug yourself in like a cheap toaster and start browning bread.

"But what if I fail?" Oh, *absolutely*. You'll fail spectacularly. You'll flop around like a fish having an existential crisis. And then—plot twist—you'll try again. Because the alternative is sitting in this exact spot six months from now, except now you're bitter *and* unmotivated. That's not a glow-up, that's just adding seasoning to the stagnation.

You think every masterpiece was born from someone jumping out of bed at 5 AM, visions dancing in their head? Please. Half the Mona Lisa was probably painted on days Leonardo wanted to yeet himself into the Arno. The work happened anyway.

So here's your mission, should you choose to accept it—and spoiler, you don't have a choice because time marches on regardless—do one small, ridiculous thing today. Not the *whole* thing. Not perfectly. Just... *start* badly. Start so badly that future you looks back and laughs. Because future you will be too busy *doing* to care.

The couch will still be there when you're done. It loves you unconditionally. It'll wait.

Now go. Your mediocre first attempt is waiting, and honestly? It's lonely without you.<|im_end|>
